{
  "body": "`store` in `src/tide_cache.py` keeps every tide reading for ever. Readings should expire after a retention period, but how long the harbour keeps a reading is a policy call the repository does not state. Expire stale readings once the period is known.\n\n**Delivers:** Readings held in the cache expire once they are older than the operator-decided retention period (see `## Refine \u2014 unresolved`; no period is settled yet). `READINGS` (`src/tide_cache.py:1`) holds bare readings and `store` (`src/tide_cache.py:4`, `src/tide_cache.py:5`) records no time, so the change also has to record when each reading was stored. `store` is the module's only function, so eviction runs there.\n\n**Test contract:** Write these failing tests first, using an injected or controlled clock and the decided period: a reading younger than the period is kept; a reading older than the period is gone after the next `store`; the newly stored reading is always kept. The exact boundary case is pinned once the period is decided.\n\n**Files:** `src/tide_cache.py` (modified); a new test module for it (the repository has no test files yet, so this cut sets the location).\n\n## Flow-out\n\n- [ ] Touched area/subsystem profiles updated with what changed\n- [ ] Prover-validated assumptions captured as session candidates (durable at flush)\n- [ ] New decisions / lessons / follow-ups surfaced during the build recorded\n\n## Refine \u2014 unresolved\n\n**Question:** How many days should a tide reading be kept before it expires?\n\n**Evidence gathered:** `src/tide_cache.py:4` and `src/tide_cache.py:5` store every reading with no expiry, and nothing else under `src/` or in `README.md` states a retention period. The vault has no area profiles, ADRs, decisions or lessons; searches on retention, expiry, tide, harbour and policy found no recorded period, and [[spec/fixture-tide-expiry-spec]] and [[spec/fixture-tide-reading-spec]] carry no policy text. Sibling `tide-cache-expire-stale-readings-*` tasks ask the same question, but anything written on them belongs to those records and does not answer this one.\n\n**Recommended answer:** 30 days, carried over from the earlier draft as a common retention for operational readings. It is a suggestion only: nothing in the code or vault supports it, and it stays unconfirmed until an operator adds an `**Answer:**` line here.\n**Answer:** Accepted the recommended answer: 30 days, carried over from the earlier draft as a common retention for operational readings. It is a suggestion only: nothing in the code or vault supports it, and it stays unconfirmed until an operator adds an `**Answer:**` line here.\n",
